WEBVTT

1
00:00:04.102 --> 00:00:08.822
In this video you’ll check your map the way your team will see it, then publish it

2
00:00:08.822 --> 00:00:09.915
so they can use it.

3
00:00:10.368 --> 00:00:12.794
Open your map from the Maps page.

4
00:00:13.245 --> 00:00:16.063
Everything you do in the editor saves as a draft.

5
00:00:16.063 --> 00:00:18.536
Your team doesn’t see it until you publish.

6
00:00:18.536 --> 00:00:21.699
The Publish button shows if your changes are published.

7
00:00:22.151 --> 00:00:28.180
First, choose Preview. This is exactly what your employees will see.

8
00:00:28.634 --> 00:00:37.925
Try it like they would. Search for a space, like 1B5, and the map shows where it is.

9
00:00:38.377 --> 00:00:40.786
Check the other floors with the tabs at the bottom.

10
00:00:41.238 --> 00:00:46.044
If something needs fixing, choose Back to editing.

11
00:00:46.497 --> 00:00:49.258
When it looks right, choose Publish.

12
00:00:49.258 --> 00:00:51.713
Your team now sees this version.

13
00:00:52.163 --> 00:00:55.741
If you change the map later, the button says Publish changes.

14
00:00:55.741 --> 00:01:00.081
Your team keeps seeing the last published version until you publish again.

15
00:01:00.532 --> 00:01:04.702
Choose Publish changes when you’re ready.

16
00:01:05.153 --> 00:01:08.603
Back on the Maps page, the map shows as published.

17
00:01:09.053 --> 00:01:13.659
Each site holds up to five maps, and one of them can be published at a time.

18
00:01:13.659 --> 00:01:17.719
You can keep the others as spare layouts, for example for an event.
